---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="About this draft">
  <header class="page-heading"><h1>A starting point<br />we can build together.</h1><p>The CpE Starter Toolkit is an RDC-led resource for beginner Computer Engineering students. This repository is the first implementation draft of the proposed project.</p></header>
  <article class="prose">
    <h2>What this version is</h2><p>Version {site.version} is a working website for content review and club contribution. It includes a proposed Windows setup path, a readiness checklist, C/C++ and Python verification programs, Git/GitHub basics, brief Mac notes, troubleshooting, a learning roadmap, and downloadable source materials.</p>
    <h2>What still needs review</h2><ul><li><strong>Department/faculty confirmation:</strong> the exact toolchain, Python series and patch version, editor extensions, minimum device requirements, and supported platforms.</li><li><strong>Device testing:</strong> a clean installation walkthrough on the proposed Windows devices, with versions and outcomes recorded.</li><li><strong>Student pilot:</strong> independent use by beginner volunteers, followed by revisions to unclear steps. No student completion results have been collected.</li><li><strong>Publication:</strong> approved free hosting and a final content/accessibility review.</li><li><strong>Long-term upkeep:</strong> annual review, club turnover, and eventual migration into the CpE Digital Hub when it is ready.</li></ul><p>The original proposal named December 11, 2026 as its intended launch deadline and an 80% pilot completion target among eligible testers. These are proposed goals, not achieved outcomes or a confirmed current schedule.</p>
    <h2>How your progress is stored</h2><p>Optional guide and readiness checkmarks are saved in browser local storage. They stay on this browser and site address. There is no student sign-in, cloud sync, analytics, or tracking service. Search loads a static index from this site; your query is filtered in the browser and is not submitted to a search service.</p><p>Links to GitHub and official software websites take you to external services with their own practices. GitHub issues and contributions can be public. Clear this site's browser data or use “Reset my progress” on the overview to remove your stored checkmarks.</p>
    <h2>Help improve a step</h2><p>You do not need to be an experienced developer to contribute. A clearer sentence, a reproducible installation problem, or an accessibility fix is useful work.</p><ul><li><a href={`${site.repository}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>Read the contribution guide</a></li><li><a href={`${site.repository}/issues/new/choose`}>Report a problem or propose an improvement</a></li><li><a href={`${site.repository}/blob/main/docs/review-status.md`}>See the technical review checklist</a></li><li><a href={`${site.repository}/blob/main/docs/pilot-testing.md`}>Use the pilot-testing template</a></li></ul>
    <h2>Credits and source material</h2><p>Project context comes from the CpE Starter Toolkit implementation proposal for AY 2026–2027 supplied by the project owner. The owner also supplied the chapter logo, administration banner, and brand-book reference. The logo and banner are used intact; Unbounded and Manrope are self-hosted through their open font packages.</p><p>Official references are listed with each guide. The exact HK Modular display font was not supplied; Unbounded provides the draft's display typography. Content and interface implementation choices were delegated by the owner.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
